{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1525161-thyrsus-crossover-chronicle-to-find-the-original-wound-father-wolfs-grave-\u2026","id":1525161,"title":"Thyrsus crossover chronicle to find the original Wound (Father Wolfs grave)\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-07T05:59:59-08:00","id":1525161,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Thyrsus crossover chronicle to find the original Wound (Father Wolfs grave)\u2026","content":"How would you guys start the story, would the Pure Tribes be more willing to get involved, what enemies would the players make chasing such a mystery and how do you think that resurrecting Father Wolf would impact the world???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T08:00:32-08:00","id":1525164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1525161-thyrsus-crossover-chronicle-to-find-the-original-wound-father-wolfs-grave-\u2026#post1525161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you guys start the story, would the Pure Tribes be more willing to get involved, what enemies would the players make chasing such a mystery and how do you think that resurrecting Father Wolf would impact the world???</div> </div> </div> </div>Too big of a setting change, at Archimages-get-involved-overtly levels of impact.<br /> <br /> <br /> IF it can be done it has to be done by high powered characters, it simply can not work otherwise with the implicit setting changes (Border Marches return? What happens with the Shadow? Do other Pangaeans still exist/return? What would Luna do? Do the Exarchs favour or oppose the change? Does the God-Machine intervine?\u200b)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T08:39:22-08:00","id":1525165,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting Father Wolf would result in an apocalypse. Father Wolf was powerful enough able to keep the balance between mortals and spirits for the entire world by himself. If he returned to a world with the Gauntlet, he would be livid. If Luna agrees to help him take down the Gauntlet, it massively escalates the threat. If she opposes him, everyone will be caught in the crossfire. Either way, you are involving the spirit who inspired the creation of the word lunatic.<br /> <br /> Anyone who made meaningful progress would draw the personal attention of The Nemesis, since this actively endangers his domain of keeping humans ignorant to the consequences their actions have on the Shadow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Signs of Sorcery, page 14</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most individuals, even those who\u2019ve made opposing the Tyrants their life\u2019s work, are beneath the Exarchs\u2019 notice, but when direct intervention does happen, it comes swiftly, without warning, and with apocalyptic brutality. An individual Pentacle mage might be the sworn enemy of a dozen Pylons for decades without Supernal incident, unknowingly cross a line one day that makes a true nuisance of herself, and be murdered by hostile Supernal entities within hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the changes would massively affect the Material World and have to deeply damage an Exarch's power base, it would also draw the attention of archmages, escalating the chronicle to the Imperial Mystery level. Those that serve the throne, those that want to permanently defeat an Exarch, archmages that argue Father Wolf's idea of balance would be beneficial to humanity, etc.<br /> <br /> A way to start such a chronicle is to create rumors of an Omphalos Stone that allows one to see the moment of Father Wolf's death. Since the world before the Gauntlet is hidden by a Lacuna, it makes it a world class treasure for the Awakened. So scholars would jump at the chance to examine it, while others might see it as a great way to bargain for massive boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T09:05:27-08:00","id":1525166,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest ignoring the Archmaster/Exarch level stuff. Like, most mages simply aren't going to be aware of it. All you need to know is that <i>someone</i> in that sphere is holding the others back from simply erasing the PCs from existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1525161-thyrsus-crossover-chronicle-to-find-the-original-wound-father-wolfs-grave-\u2026?p=1525165#post1525165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A way to start such a chronicle is to create rumors of an Omphalos Stone that allows one to see the moment of Father Wolf's death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the implication that it'd be Father Wolf's heart?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T12:12:03-08:00","id":1525174,"title":"","content":"I'm not a Mage person, I'm a werewolf person, and coming at this from that perspective.<br /> <br /> I think I'd come at this sideways. I wouldn't put the PCs on the mystery of trying to resurrect Father Wolf, I think I'd come at it sideways, the PCs would begin investigating something seemingly small and slowly come to see the big picture that someone is trying to resurrect Father Wolf. Other forces are opposing them. Other forces are using both sides. Other forces are trying to benefit from the other forces all doing stuff and don't actually care about Father Wolf at all. Make it a huge web, maybe a conspiracy (from Deviant) wants Father Wolf's Omphalos Stone to create super powerful Deviants while some high primal urge werewolf believes it is the key to resurrecting Father Wolf, while some random spirits are enjoying the fighting between the Uratha and the conspiracy. Then have the PCs end up with an important piece in the middle of everything and no idea who, if anyone, they should trust or support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> would the Pure Tribes be more willing to get involved </div> </div> </div>I imagine all the Uratha tribes would have people involved in some way, shape, or form or another. And each tribe would have members on both sides, for and against it. No single tribe, not even among the Pure, would be entirely for it. Especially, ESPECIALLY, if it is a human (aka Mage) doing it. The Prey Must Not Know, it's a rule for the Pure as much as it is for the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what enemies would the players make chasing such a mystery\u200b </div> </div> </div>Everything, up to and including some gods. Look at how powerful Rank 6+ spirits can be. Look at how powerful Hosts can grow to be, especially the one that Chris Allen designed in the Werewolf forum. All of those beings are going to be especially interested in Father Wolf not returning. So is pretty much everyone else in the universe. I don't even know if the Underworld or any of it's gods would want Father Wolf to come back. <br /> <br /> Mummies and Vampires, IIRC, are too new to have been around in Father Wolf's time, but mummies don't experience time linearly so maybe some have encountered him. Some of the True Fey might have been around when he was, they were kidnapping people and making Lost back then, so I doubt they would be too excited about his return, but also he didn't specifically hunt them. The God Machine may or may not have existed at that time, it probably did, but it's very interested in the status quo, so it's probably against Father Wolf's return. <br /> <br /> I think the Hunters would have the most interesting reactions. Father Wolf didn't hunt people, mostly, but he's powerful on a scale that the Vigil cannot fathom, I can't imagine them thinking it's worth the risk, even though he would be an ally in a lot of ways. <br /> <br /> Just as an aside, imagine if Father Wolf returned to life, not as a Pangean but as a Promethean... I'm imagining a few things here, 1 is it basically taking the whole of the Pyros in the world to animate him, and him over flowing with it, flaming eyes, flaming mouth, a monster of both life and creation. But I'm also imagining Father Wolf trying to do the pilgrimage and learn what it means to be human, him wearing an apron and vaccuuming an apartment (or the forest), him signing checks with a pen held in his massive jaws to pay the light bill....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T15:53:44-08:00","id":1525181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1525161-thyrsus-crossover-chronicle-to-find-the-original-wound-father-wolfs-grave-\u2026?p=1525166#post1525166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest ignoring the Archmaster/Exarch level stuff. Like, most mages simply aren't going to be aware of it. All you need to know is that <i>someone</i> in that sphere is holding the others back from simply erasing the PCs from existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is the implication that it'd be Father Wolf's heart?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not considered that option, but its wonderfully thematic and would definitely be the type of thing that would start a race for the artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T20:16:34-08:00","id":1525189,"title":"","content":"Worth remembering that the hearts of Pangaeans are huge \u2014 the <i>pieces</i> of them used to make the Omphalos Stones were twice the height of a person \u2014 and resurrecting a Pangaean is as &quot;simple&quot; as putting the (stone) heart back in the (flesh) body, which necessitates a heart that is at least mostly whole and a body that still at least partially exists.<br /> <br /> The Hosts have, by fairly direct implication, been trying something similar (albeit not totally identical) for the last several thousand years with various workarounds and questionable degrees of success, and while the process of rot for a Pangaean corpse is stated to take centuries there <i>is</i> a time limit, however loosely stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T00:48:35-08:00","id":1525194,"title":"","content":"I would add that <i>The </i><i>Sundered World</i> is fairly explicit that Wolf's death wasn't just a contingent event, it was indicative of a changing world. Like, even comparatively small groups of humans becoming agriculturalists were apparently too much disruption to Wolf. In the present you'd be bringing them back to a world where those processes have engulfed the planet.<br /> <br /> Not to say it can't be done; merely that you should probably need something a bit stronger than simply returning his heart (even though as Satchel says, that's probably not possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T03:10:53-08:00","id":1525200,"title":"","content":"The story behind Ravening Wolf could be a relevant precedent. He's a Firstborn who died long before modern times - possibly before the Sundering or soon after. His rotting corpse was hidden in the spiritual vicinity of Mongolia. Recently, one of the Forsaken ended up discovering and consuming his body, and is now slowly transforming into Ravening Wolf reborn, even creating a burgeoning Tribe (still a Lodge) around him. It's unclear what manner of being he's becoming, but it's likely he will be adapted to the modern metaphysics, Gauntlet and all.<br /> <br /> A chance to become an avatar of Father Wolf, or knowing that someone else is about to, would send entire Lodges and Tribes into a frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T01:06:13-08:00","id":1525340,"title":"","content":"From a mage perspective, chances are if you are doing this - and not Archmasters yourselves - you are working (whether you know it or not) for an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Maybe Fate is conspiring to lead you to this act which will alter the world (entirely something an Archmaster would do to leave her imprint on the world and change the supernal - though likely aligned with the faction of Archmasters who want to return the Supernal Gods to the Supernal, this doesn't necessarily perfectly align with their goals).<br /> <br /> Maybe one of the party members is an Ochema of the Archmaster (shared soul, but independently thinking while in a different realm).<br /> <br /> Given the above comments, maybe the party has to try and undo some of the changes which lead to the Sundering (ie farming) as a necessary step in the ressurection, perhaps taking down global communications would be seen as an attack on panopticon, and the mages are onboard because it is anti-Exarches...<br /> <br /> Maybe it doesn't require returning the earth to a pre-Sundering state, but the ressurection will dramatically alter what Father Wolf is...<br /> <br /> Maybe there is some entity in the Underworld which is like a ghost of Father Wolf, and (corpse or not) is required for the ressurection to work. They are likely either a Cthonic entity of immense power and very difficult to negotiate with, or appear as a withered ghost inhabiting a Dominion which will slowly gain power as it gets closer to the Shadow and free of the Old Laws, or a Kerberos enforcing laws (by hunting) on the spirits and ghosts it finds within its Dominion.<br /> <br /> Or maybe this entity in the Underworld is a red herring, and Fate directed you down there to teach you something about the nature of death and you merely return with new information....<br /> <br /> Maybe (CtL) Arcadia is the key, the Gentry are after all in some ways outside of time, and changelings often return to find time has moved differently, thus this offers a way to go back and get parts of necessary for the ressurection (the Ophalmos stone, corpse, anything else?) Except you have to deal with the Gentry... Who are liable to screw you over with any possible deal you strike. Maybe the Gentry can make contracts with actual aspects of reality and you don't need to go back in time to alter things... You just need to alter reality... But again, dealing with the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Maybe really you should be looking at the gods of the Shadow. Luna in particular has an interest, but most Totem spirits have an interest in werewolf stuff. And there must be some spirit of the Hunt. Maybe they just want to return the world to a Hunting based economy, and will end up going from God ranked spirit to something embodied. Maybe this isn't Father Wolf (unless you add memories from the Underworld) but is still close enough, and will require dramatically altering the world to achieve - this is really werewolf stuff that I'm not too familiar with.<br /> <br /> And that is to entirely ignore the Astral, the Anima Mundi in particular and the Archetype of the Hunter? The Supernal, and any potential Supernal Gods bound/fallen who might be associated with Father Wolf in some way, Mummy related time travel Shenanigans (or maybe one of the artifacts is a relic in a mummy's tomb), or the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"typos) 11-11-2023, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:09:13-08:00","id":1526749,"title":"","content":"What direction did this campaign end up taking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T10:20:41-08:00","id":1526863,"title":"","content":"One possible start could be of one of the players, sometime in the distant past, having stumbled across what (at the time) they thought was naught but a fancy bauble of a rock/gem/crystal/some-similarly-long-term-lasting-substance-or-item. After they became an Urathra, they <i>do</i> notice that essence seems to flow oddly around it, but don't realise its true importance until they become sufficiently powerful &amp;/or skilled to 'unlock' the required perception check. Upon passing it, they (begin to) realise the truth, &amp; you can start that part of the chronicle. Perhaps, as a subtle clue, essence manipulation gets a boost while wearing/holding the 'bauble'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T07:32:04-08:00","id":1526925,"title":"","content":"I would just start with Mysteries involving ghost warriors, like the Wild Hunt and the Nightmarchers. Not only are they now able to invade the Shadow, but they are taking lupine aspects over time. These &quot;corrupting super Anchors&quot; would be pieces of the Omphalos stone. Father Wolf was so powerful that just having a fragment of it Resonate with his death is enough to have this effect.<br /> <br /> But then why were spirits not affected ? Maybe wherever they are stored is warded, weird, better look into that....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}